  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform wooden stick of mass 1.6 kg and length <math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> rests in an inclined manner on a smooth, vertical wall of height h <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> such that a small portion of the stick extends beyond the wall. The reaction force of the wall on the stick is perpendicular to the stick. The stick makes an angle of <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> with the wall and the bottom of the stick is on a rough floor. The reaction of the wall on the stick is equal in magnitude to the reaction of the floor on the stick. The ratio h/ <math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and the frictional force f at the bottom of the stick are: <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
